      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Nick / from United Kingdom",
      "description": "The position has been constructed against a rocky crag using local rock to build a wall front and sides, and steel rails that are likely to have come from the narrow gauge railway between Camber Point fuel depot and Moody Brook radio station.\nCorrugated iron sheet nearby suggests this was also used to weatherproof the shelter.\n\nI have called this a command post because of the large size and both the effort and materials that have been used to construct it. It could also have served as an observation post due to the commanding views over the ground to its front.",
      "dateCreated": "2021-03-07 16:39",
      "categories": [
        "2021 in the Falkland Islands",
        "Battle of Mount Longdon",
        "CC-BY-2.0",
        "Camber Railway",
